description: Conventions when changing the Python engine
globs: p1401/**/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

# Engine (`p1401/`)

- Keep Windows and Linux on the same modules; OS-specific I/O belongs in dedicated helpers
  (`linuxusb.py`, `linuxroot.py`, `rawdisk.py`, etc.), not forked business rules
- Rules that mutate `config.plist` are recorded in the build result; name them clearly
- Downloads: exact URL, size, SHA-256; refuse mismatches
- Prefer plain "why" comments over narrating the code
- After rule / kext / `engine.py` / `nullmoth.py` changes, run the hardware corpus when feasible
- Unit tests: `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t . -p 'test_*.py'`
